course: dictionary
lesson: 15720
title: Tragically: a sad word
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Tragically is an adverb, so it tells you how something happened. It means in a very sad way, usually because someone died or something terrible happened. «The brave dog tragically lost its way in the storm.» The word tragically tells you that the loss is serious and sad.
explain: Writers often put tragically at the start of a sentence to warn you that bad news is coming. «Tragically, nobody survived the flood.» Before you read on, you already know the news will be serious and sad.
explain: Ask yourself: did something terrible happen? If it did, tragically may fit. Check by reading the sentence again with your meaning in place of the word. If it still makes sense, you have worked it out.
fact: Tragically means in a very sad way.
fact: It is usually used when someone died or something terrible happened.
fact: «Tragically, nobody survived.» At the start of a sentence, it warns the reader that sad news is coming.
fact: Phrases you may see in history and news include «tragically died» and «tragically short life».
fact: In a joke, tragically can make a small problem sound huge: «Tragically, the shop had run out of chocolate.» This is informal and silly.
exercise: «The ship tragically sank in the cold sea.» What does tragically mean here? | In a fast and happy way | In a quiet way, like a whisper | Funny, like a joke | *In a very sad way, because something terrible happened
exercise: «Tragically, the shop had run out of chocolate.» Is this about a terrible event? | Yes, the news is very serious | *No, it is a joke that makes a small disappointment sound huge | Yes, a whole town was lost | Yes, someone was badly hurt
exercise: Where does an author often put tragically to warn the reader? | Never in a sentence | *At the start of a sentence | Only in poems | At the end of a sentence only
test: «The young king tragically died in the war.» What does tragically tell you? | The king was happy and healthy | *The death was very sad and terrible | The war was a game | The king was very old and wise
test: Dad says, «Tragically, the bus was late again.» Why is Dad using tragically? | *He is joking, and makes a small problem sound huge | Dad is writing a history book | Someone was hurt on the bus | He is telling a serious story
exam: Which sentence uses tragically for a serious, sad event? | «Tragically, we played in the park.» | «Tragically, I ate my lunch quickly.» | *«Tragically, the old bridge collapsed and people were lost.» | «Tragically, the sun is yellow.»
